text:
@Mehffortsource; *Trust me bro* 

*No really trust me, I’m Anti-China so I definitely know!* 

*Also Gordon Chang and China Uncensored since I’m a brainwashed schmuck* 🤕🤡

@autogefuehl Thank you for the response! I am sure that there are good quality fake leather, i just haven't seen it yet. I still prefer cloth. I just only have my own Model 3 to compare it to, which is awful and i have had replaced both seat and steering wheel fabric before 40.000km which have made me a little worried of "vegan leather" as the Model 3 is the first time i've experienced it, and it has been an awful experience. Even the seats and wheel they replaced, also have issues so i might need it replaced for a second time...

However, i think the issue is that the website in Denmark, and all reviews say "Leather" not "Leatherette" or "Vegan leather" etc. which i am pretty sure it is illegal to call something leather if it is not. Everyone, including BYD sales staff and all reviewers in Denmark think it's real leather.

I'm not so much disappointed it isn't real leather if it is good quality, i also prefer not to kill cows if possible, so it's only positive if it's very good quality vegan leather. I'm more concerned with BYD making such a large mistake if it is actually not leather, i wonder where else they have labeled wrong. I have ordered a Byd Seal to replace my Model 3 so i hope i get what it says on the ordering slip with everything else and they didn't mislabel more things.

@autogefuehl Thank you again for the in depth research. I will assume it's vegan then. I was sure leather was a protected term in Europe when so many other things are. Feta, champagne etc. Maybe it's more about being misleading than being wrong. I also assume in 2023 more people prefer to have animal-free interiors, so if it actually is animal free, i would assume they would highlight that like many other companies do, very strange.

Unfortunately, my wallet doesn't allow me to sit inside a modern high end BMW haha :) So all experiences i have is with cloth seats, leather from a 2010's Audi, and then Model 3 Vegan leather. Maybe i'm just weird but so far i still prefer cloth over real leather- Cloth looks worse but i feel the durability and feel of sitting is the best.

Lets see about the Seal when i go test drive it in November. So far i only heard good things about the seats. In the end i don't care about the material, i just want them to be good.

@autogefuehl Yeah all this confusion actually only made me more comfortable with the fact that if they're vegan, people can't tell.

I do however think it's a little worrying that BYD doesn't even seem to know. Doesn't show the best knowledge/attention to detail maybe. Makes me a little worried about what other mistakes and wrong info they might have said. What if there is some other feature that i wanted with the car, that isn't there, or is different. 

Both BYD Denmark, as well as the BYD Dealer where i ordered the car from, are all very nice and responds to questions, so that is good at least.

@autogefuehl Thank you for the update, appreciate the effort! BYD Denmark kept saying animal leather, so i kinda had to assume so when they went so heavy with the "leather seats" in their marketing. I went to test drive the car and honestly it was hard to tell. They were very good seats though.

I actually ordered a Seal and there has been so much confusion about so many things, i am not really surprised there was confusion about the seats either. Multiple features, tyre/rim sizes, tow hook, delivery dates, payment etc. is all confused by BYD and the dealers. The tow hook BYD made a mistake on the COC document, so they had to cancel all orders with tow hook and push them back to summer 2024 when they have corrected the COC for the newer shipments. The 2023 - Summer 2024 cars won't ever be able to get a tow hook. I really liked the car, but communication/information i am not impressed by.

I think it's kinda weird/uncommon to market leather seats as a feature in 2023, especially on an EV. I would assume most people would want vegan at this point. But yeah the biggest disappointment is that it seems that EU/Germany got marketed vegan leather, and Denmark (maybe other countries too?) got marketed animal leather.

@martingicemi8745 It has nothing to do with racism. Don't you follow news? China is a socialist state and basically all chinese companies are on state's leash. Money and all the data that the companies gather go to the state. By supporting Chinese companies you basically support China and its actions.Have you heard about Uyghur genocide in China that's happening as we speak? Or how they track and grade their own citizens? Does Huawei ring any bells? Huawei's internet technology has basically been banned in US because of spying.
I guess if I condemned Russia's war against Ukraine, you would call that racist too. In that logic all the sanctions and restrictions by US and EU against Russia are also just racism...
Critisism does not equal racism. You should know that.

@autogefuehl that will ”seal” the deal then.
Need a comprehensive comparison test also.
Much Love!

@dannytq founded in the same year 2003, they introduced their first ever model's in the same year 2008. 
Nothing imo shows byd is any kind of match for tesla SMDH. Not in perf, not safety, not tech, not ui, not charging, not in efficiency etc. 
The seal isn't even equal to a 2017 model 3 and that's some simple FACTS. 😎
